        <a href="/membership" class="btn-sol primary">Join to unlock member pricing →</a>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-light); margin-top:0.5rem;">ArmorVita and NeuroBridge are available at member pricing — see <a href="/membership">/membership</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="path-card path-rx">
      <div class="path-badge path-badge-rx">Rx Protocol</div>
      <h3>Comprehensive 4M Consult</h3>
      <p class="path-price">Full peptide candidacy review</p>
      <p>Ready to start peptide protocols — Semax, Selank, BPC-157, Sermorelin, CJC-1295/Ipamorelin, Tesamorelin, MK-677. One consult covers nootropic + GH peptides, body composition, lab review, and your full personalized 4M plan via our contracted licensed telemedicine practice.</p>
      <a href="/consult" class="btn-sol secondary">Schedule Rx Consult →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── When to choose which ── -->
  <div class="when-strip">
    <div class="when-col">
      <div class="when-label">Start with OTC foundation when:</div>
      <p>Exploring foundational support before committing to peptide protocols — build the substrate stack first and give peptides the best environment to work in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="when-divider"></div>
    <div class="when-col">
      <div class="when-label">Go Rx when:</div>
      <p>Ready to start peptide protocols with lab data, medical oversight, and pharmacy-grade compounded peptides — not research-chemical sourcing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Protégé footer card ── -->
  <div class="protege-card">
    <strong>Want the deeper protocol?</strong> The 4M Protégé program includes ongoing peptide protocol monitoring, lab review cadence, and coaching — not just a one-time consult. <a href="/consult">Learn about Protégé →</a>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Peptide reference cards ── -->
  <h2>Peptide Categories</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Nootropic Peptides</h3>
      <p><em>Cognitive performance + brain protection</em></p>
      <ul style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-light);">
